 in log-transformed age-adjusted mortality rates were assessed in Joinpoint software\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"by performing a sequence of permutation tests using Monte Carlo sampling and the Bonferroni correction for multiple testing\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"were generated by industry and occupation for men and women and adjusted for 5-year age groups and race\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"CIs were calculated assuming Poisson distribution of the data.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Age-adjusted death rates were calculated by applying age-specific death rates to the 2000 U.S. Census standard population age distribution.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}